Data

The data come from the Higher Education Research and Development (HERD)
Survey, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering
Statistics (NCSES) at the U.S. National Science Foundation. The source
files are public, institution-level microdata published by NCSES:
https://ncses.nsf.gov/explore-data/microdata/higher-education-research-development

HERD Explorer reshapes and combines those files but does not change the
reported values.

For context, the database also holds data from other publishers, kept in
tables named context_* and listed with their sources on the site's About HERD
page (data.html#data) and in the database's sources table:

- Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education, 2021 update and
  2025 public data files, American Council on Education
  (https://carnegieclassifications.acenet.edu). Licensed under a Creative
  Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/). HERD Explorer uses it
  for institution types and groups (context_carnegie_2021,
  context_carnegie_2025, and the Carnegie columns of institution_groups and
  the downloads); those derived tables are shared under the same license, for
  noncommercial use. It is not covered by the Apache License.
- Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS), National Center for
  Education Statistics, U.S. Department of Education: faculty and staff,
  enrollment, completions, finance and locations.
- Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering
  (GSS), NCSES, U.S. National Science Foundation.
- EPSCoR eligibility, U.S. National Science Foundation.
- State population estimates, U.S. Census Bureau.
- GDP price deflator and state GDP, U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis.
- Changes in Federal Research Requirements Since 1991, Council on
  Governmental Relations (COGR).

U.S. federal data are in the public domain. Neither NCSES nor any of these
publishers is responsible for this project, and errors in the reshaping and
combining are this project's own. Report them on the AI4RA Groups.io
listserv with #DataScience in the subject line:
https://groups.ai4ra.uidaho.edu/g/main

